 libpve-storage-perl (9.1.26) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * iscsi: only scan for newly added LUNs when activating an iSCSI
     storage with existing sessions, instead of running a full 'iscsiadm
     --rescan' that revalidates every known LUN path every ten seconds.
     This stops periodic ALUA kernel log floods and request-queue freezes
     during disk revalidation while still discovering new LUNs
     automatically. Growing an existing iSCSI LUN now requires running
     'iscsiadm -m session --rescan' (or per-path 'device/rescan') on each
     node, matching Fibre Channel.
